This repository builds Skate 3 Recomp, the native recompilation of the
Xbox 360 version of Skate 3 by mchughalex, for ARM64 Linux:
https://github.com/mchughalex/skate3recomp
Skate 3 Recomp publishes no licence; it is not stored here. The scripts
download it (and its fork of the ReXGlue SDK) from its own repositories at
build time, at the commit in upstream.json, and the patches in patches/game
and patches/sdk change it on your machine. Nothing built from it is
published here: you build the game yourself from your own copy.

ReXGlue SDK: https://github.com/rexglue/rexglue-sdk
Copyright (c) 2026, Tom Clay, with portions derived from the Xenia project
(Copyright (c) 2022, Ben Vanik and Xenia project contributors).
The posix fault fixes and the shader math change in patches/sdk come from
the FIFA Street ARM64 port (https://github.com/Ken5998/fifa-street-arm64)
by the same author; the shader math is ported from shiftglue-sdk
(https://github.com/arcanite24/shiftglue-sdk), under the ReXGlue SDK's
license.

Dear ImGui: https://github.com/ocornut/imgui, Copyright (c) 2014-2026 Omar
Cornut, MIT License. patches/imgui changes it at build time.

The disc image is read with xiso_extract from Saints Reborn
(https://github.com/whompay/SaintsReborn, Copyright 2026 Whompay, Apache
License 2.0), downloaded at build time at the commit and checksum in
upstream.json; it is not stored here.

Skate 3 is a trademark of Electronic Arts. This project is not affiliated
with Electronic Arts or Microsoft. No game files are included: you need your
own Xbox 360 copy of Skate 3.
